WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.103
Threat hunting is not magic and it is not guesswork.

2
00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:13.430
Effective hunters combine curiosity, analytical thinking, technical knowledge, understanding of attacker behaviors, and familiarity with organizational environments.

3
00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:21.682
Hunting complements SIEM operations, EDR investigations, incident response, threat intelligence, and detection engineering.

4
00:00:21.682 --> 00:00:23.987
It does not replace those capabilities.

5
00:00:23.987 --> 00:00:30.332
Instead, it helps teams move from only reacting to alerts toward actively searching for hidden threats.

6
00:00:30.332 --> 00:00:35.960
A healthy hunting discipline values evidence, documentation, repeatable methods, and feedback.

7
00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:44.690
Hunters should be able to explain the hypothesis, data sources, search approach, findings, confidence level, and recommended next steps.

8
00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:51.725
Over time, a mature hunting capability improves resilience, detection quality, and operational awareness.

9
00:00:51.725 --> 00:00:58.839
It helps organizations learn what normal looks like, where visibility is weak, and where defenders should improve controls.
